# Drafted by Gemini (R25 endings), edited.

~ start
Narrator: At the end of all things, you took the hand Kehlenn offered, and the moon fell like a millstone upon every other soul in Druskenvald.
Narrator: The hills, the clocktower, and the timber roofs of Wickermoor dissolve beneath the impact into a vast, surging tide of green light.
Narrator: Only the four of you float untouched upon that deep sea of raw rebirth, drifting where an entire realm used to stand.
Narrator: Below your feet, the unshaped spirit of the valley waits like wet clay for your word to give it form.
if flag.moonfall_realm == "wild"
Narrator: At your command, great untamed forests burst upward from the green tide, tangling into a boundless wild of moss and ancient horn.
endif
if flag.moonfall_realm == "city"
Narrator: At your command, pale stone towers and bright glass lanterns rise from the deep, forming a shining city that knows no country dark.
endif
if flag.moonfall_realm == "farm"
Narrator: At your command, the tide settles into gentle hills of golden wheat and quiet orchards, warm with the smell of turned earth.
endif
if flag.moonfall_realm == "home"
Narrator: At your command, the mist takes the familiar shape of the homeland you lost in life, rebuilt from memory upon the quiet deep.
endif
Narrator: A new world hardens beneath your boots, silent and vast, built upon the drowned silence of the old.
the_vagrant [weary]: It is a grand thing to shape a realm from the flood, though the water stays deep underneath.
-> END
